---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {SINS} from '../lib/sins';
import {questions,CHOICES} from '../lib/scoring';
import {icon} from '../lib/art';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebPage','@id':new URL('#webpage',Astro.site!).href,name:'7 Deadly Sins Test',url:Astro.site!.href,description:'A free personality-themed entertainment test using 35 public-domain IPIP items, mapped to seven independently scored themes.',inLanguage:'en',isPartOf:{'@type':'WebSite','@id':new URL('#website',Astro.site!).href,name:'Seven Sins',url:Astro.site!.href}};
---
<Layout>
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}/>
<section class="test-section wrap" aria-labelledby="test-title">
<div class="intro" id="intro">
<h1 id="test-title">7 Deadly Sins Test</h1>
<p class="intro-copy">Which of the seven deadly sins is strongest in you?</p>
<p class="test-facts">35 questions <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Free <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> No sign-up</p>

</div>
<div class="quiz-area" id="quiz-area">
<form class="questionnaire" id="quiz" aria-labelledby="question-heading">
<div class="quiz-topline"><span id="question-counter">Question 1 <span class="muted">/ 35</span></span><span class="private-note"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="10" width="14" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg> Answers stay on this device</span></div>
<div class="progress-track" role="progressbar" aria-label="Questions answered" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="35" aria-valuenow="0" id="progress"><div id="progress-fill" class="progress-segments"><span><i style="background:#8260cf"></i></span><span><i style="background:#d69b22"></i></span><span><i style="background:#df5d78"></i></span><span><i style="background:#378867"></i></span><span><i style="background:#d57a35"></i></span><span><i style="background:#ce5650"></i></span><span><i style="background:#5274bc"></i></span></div></div>
<div class="question-body"><p class="question-instruction">How accurately does this describe you?</p><h2 id="question-heading" tabindex="-1">{questions[0].text}</h2>
<fieldset class="answers" id="answers"><legend class="sr-only">Choose how accurately the statement describes you</legend>{CHOICES.map((choice,i)=><label class="answer"><input type="radio" name="answer" value={i}/><span class="answer-key" aria-hidden="true">{i+1}</span><span>{choice}</span><svg class="answer-check" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6"/></svg></label>)}</fieldset></div>
<div class="quiz-bottom"><button type="button" class="text-button" id="back" disabled><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back</button><button type="submit" class="primary-button" id="next" disabled>Continue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></div>
<p class="quiz-hint" id="quiz-hint">Go with your usual self. There are no right answers.</p>
</form>
<p class="under-quiz">Real personality items. A playful perspective.<br/><a href="/methodology/">Read about the IPIP questions and our interpretation.</a></p>
<noscript><p class="notice">Please enable JavaScript to take the test and generate your image. You can still read <a href="/methodology/">all questions and the scoring method</a>.</p></noscript>
</div>
<div id="results" class="results" hidden aria-labelledby="result-heading"></div>
</section>
<div class="below-test">
<section class="how-section wrap" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-heading"><div><h2 id="how-heading">How the 7 deadly sins test works</h2><p>This 7 deadly sins test turns your answers to 35 personality statements into a colorful snapshot of pride, greed, lust, envy, gluttony, wrath, and sloth. Answer directly above, then explore which themes stand out for you.</p></div><ol class="steps"><li><span class="step-number">1</span><div><h3>Be your usual self.</h3><p>Rate how accurately each statement describes you, rather than how you think you should answer. You can go back and change an answer.</p></div></li><li><span class="step-number">2</span><div><h3>Meet your seven sides.</h3><p>Get an independent score for every theme, your strongest result, and a short explanation. The seven percentages do not add up to 100.</p></div></li><li><span class="step-number">3</span><div><h3>Keep the picture.</h3><p>Download your personal result as a PNG or share a link. Friends can take the same test and compare their own results.</p></div></li></ol></section>
<section class="themes-section wrap" aria-labelledby="themes-heading"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="themes-heading">What the seven deadly sins mean</h2><p>Old labels, everyday patterns.<br/>A high score is a conversation starter, not a verdict.</p></div><div class="themes-list">{SINS.map(s=><article class="theme-row"><span class="theme-icon" style={`--sin-color:${s.color};--sin-pale:${s.pale}`} set:html={icon(s.id,27)}></span><h3>{s.name}<span>{s.theme}</span></h3><p>{s.description}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="how-section wrap" aria-labelledby="reading-heading"><div><h2 id="reading-heading">Read your results, beyond the strongest sin.</h2><p>Your 7 deadly sins test results include seven separate scores. Start with the strongest theme, then look at the full profile: a close second can be just as useful for reflection. A small gap between scores does not establish a meaningful psychological difference.</p><p>The chart shows each score along one sector’s radius. Read the printed percentages to compare themes; the colored areas are visual illustrations, not measurements of how much of your personality belongs to each sin.</p></div><div><h3>A score example</h3><p>Suppose pride scores 60% and sloth scores 40%. That means 12 of 20 possible points for pride and 8 of 20 for sloth after reverse scoring. It does not mean that pride makes up 60% of your character, or that your sloth is lower than 60% of other people’s.</p><h3>Make the explanation useful</h3><p>Open a theme’s explanation and think of a specific recent situation that fits, plus one that does not. Use the suggested reflection as a small experiment rather than a label. If several themes tie, the result keeps that tie instead of choosing an arbitrary winner. Read the <a href="/methodology/">complete scoring method and item key</a> for the calculation behind every result.</p></div></section>
<section class="faq-section wrap" aria-labelledby="faq-heading"><h2 id="faq-heading">Questions about the test</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>What is the 7 deadly sins test?</summary><p>It is a free entertainment questionnaire that maps your responses to seven themes from the traditional seven deadly sins. You receive a score for each theme, a strongest-theme summary, written explanations, and a downloadable image.</p></details><details><summary>Where do the personality questions come from?</summary><p>All 35 statements come directly from the <a href="https://ipip.ori.org/AlphabeticalItemList.htm">International Personality Item Pool (IPIP)</a>, whose items are in the public domain. We preserve their wording and publish the item identifiers on our <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>. Selecting these items and mapping them to seven sins is our own interpretation.</p></details><details><summary>Is this a scientifically validated psychological test?</summary><p>No. IPIP supplies personality items, but this particular selection, seven-sin mapping, and result explanations have not been validated as a psychological scale. Use the result for entertainment and self-reflection, not diagnosis, hiring, or judging someone’s character.</p></details><details><summary>What do the percentages mean?</summary><p>Each theme has five questions scored from 0 to 4, with some items scored in reverse. The total is divided by 20 and multiplied by 100. So 80% means 16 out of 20 possible points on that theme, not that you are more “sinful” than 80% of people. Several themes can score highly at once.</p></details><details><summary>Are my answers private?</summary><p>Your answers are processed and saved in this browser. The site does not send quiz responses to a server. A result link includes your seven scores, so share it only if you want others to see them. Our <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> explains local storage and hosting.</p></details><details><summary>How do I download my result image?</summary><p>Finish all 35 questions, then select Save result image beneath the chart. The site creates a 1080 × 1350 PNG containing the seven scores and strongest-theme summary. Check your browser’s Downloads folder or download manager, then save the file to your photos if you want to post it. The image is generated in your browser; no email address is required. If a download fails, keep the result open and try again.</p></details><details><summary>How can I share and compare results with friends?</summary><p>Use the green share button beside the result chart. Your browser opens its sharing options when supported, or the site copies a result link. Anyone opening that link can see the seven scores, so treat it as something you choose to make visible. Friends can take the same questionnaire and compare each theme, rather than only comparing the strongest label. A shared link contains scores, not the individual answers. Screenshotting or posting the PNG also reveals the displayed result.</p></details><details><summary>Does this quiz match an anime character or measure religious belief?</summary><p>No. The seven deadly sins are the cultural themes used to organize this personality quiz. The result does not assign an anime character, test religious knowledge, or assess beliefs. It describes responses to everyday personality statements. If you arrived looking for a character-matching game or a theology quiz, the questions and result here serve a different purpose.</p></details><details><summary>Can I retake the test or change an answer?</summary><p>Yes. Use Back while answering, or Edit answers after finishing. Start over clears your local quiz progress so you can take a fresh test. Your result may change with your answers and circumstances.</p></details></div></section>
<section class="closing-section wrap"><h2>Curious which side leads?</h2><a href="#test-title" class="primary-button">Take the test <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span></a></section>
</div>
<script>import '../lib/quiz';</script>
</Layout>
